    "narrative": "The offensive ceiling for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the matchup against the right-handed Jack Kochanowicz, but the day\u2019s standout is clearly **Corbin Carroll**. With a commanding 87.14 score, **Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against Littell. Despite a slight efficiency penalty for facing an elite hold pitcher, his combination of speed and order utility makes him the engine of our attack. **Josh Naylor** also projects as an elite pillar (78.46) in a favorable spot against Montero; he is a primary beneficiary of today\u2019s wind patterns, which add a critical 5% boost to his power profile. **Brice Turang** rounds out our top-tier plays (73.40); his projected ascension to the three-hole, paired with a significant park-factor lift, solidifies his status as an essential start.\n\nDeciding between our depth pieces required surgical precision, with **Travis Bazzana** emerging as the most difficult omission. His 50.93 score was suppressed primarily by a neutral matchup against Leiter, falling just behind the higher-upside profiles of **Henry Bolte** and **Seiya Suzuki**. While **Bazzana** offers elite order placement at the top of the lineup, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages and raw SP matchup data supporting our starters. Meanwhile, keep a close watch on **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**; as both carry \"Lineup Pending\" status, their projected scores are contingent on securing those assumed spots. Finally, monitor **Vinnie Pasquantino** (56.15); despite a strong 14% platoon edge, he faces a stiff test against Ryan\u2019s 3.19 xERA, marking him as a marginal start that requires active observation as the game approaches. **Mickey Moniak** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving no further ambiguity for our bench management strategy.",
